# fresh checkouts / git worktrees get it.
!/buckconfig.d/
!/buckconfig.d/**
!/.buckroot
!/.buckversion
!**/BUCK
!**/TARGETS
/buck-out/
/.buckcredentials
/rust-project.json
/prelude

# snowydeer deploy boundary (Phase 4) — vendored Buck2 + Python files
!/nix/snowydeer/
!/nix/snowydeer/**
# link_style constraints for snowydeer transition_to_static
!/constraints/
!/constraints/**
/.agent-wt

# Allow nested gitignores
!/**/.gitignore

# cargo-fuzz manifests and targets; generated corpora/artifacts stay ignored by
# tests/fuzz/.gitignore.
!/tests/fuzz/
!/tests/fuzz/Cargo.toml
!/tests/fuzz/Cargo.lock
!/tests/fuzz/.gitignore
!/tests/fuzz/fuzz_targets/**/*.rs
# A corpus checkout is materialized only by the flake test into one temporary
# Nix-store output; it must never become a regular workspace directory.
result/

# docs/LIMITATIONS.md L21 — the vendored `trustfall/` working copy.
#
# 21 MB carrying a nested `.git`, and the build does not use it. Root
# `Cargo.toml:137` git-pins the fork by rev
# (7e71e35715dfac561e3453c834b469a200330997), `Cargo.lock` resolves it from that
# URL, and there is no `[patch]` entry redirecting the dependency to this path —
# so cargo fetches its own copy and this directory is a developer's checkout of
# the same rev, nothing more.
#
# It is denied explicitly rather than left to chance. The blanket `/**/*` at the
# top of this file is followed by `!/**/*.rs` and `!/**/*.md`, which un-ignore
# several thousand files inside it; a single `git add -A` would therefore commit
# a foreign project's sources into this tree, and `git status` would keep
# reporting `?? trustfall/` forever in the meantime. That is the "gitlink risk"
# L21 names, and this rule is the whole fix — deliberately NOT deleting the
# directory, because it is someone's working copy of the fork and not ours to
# remove.
#
# If the fork ever needs to be built from this tree instead of fetched, the
# change is a `[patch.crates-io]` entry pointing at it, at which point this rule
# should be revisited in the same commit.
/trustfall/

# Scratch research notes; not build input, not evidence.
/workspace/docs/research/
# Captured frames from `cargo test --test screenshots` (workspace/gui). They are
# evidence, not source: regenerable in one command, and byte-unstable across
# machines because glyph rasterisation depends on the host font stack — so
# committing them would churn on every run while proving nothing a re-run
# cannot. The regeneration command lives in GUI-PROOF.md.
tests/shots/
